Three runtime crash vectors that could leave users on a blank screen or trigger silent failures in Firestore operations.

## Changes

### `src/components/ErrorBoundary.jsx` (new)
- Class component with `componentDidCatch`; renders a Japanese-language fallback UI with a reload button instead of unmounting the entire tree on any unhandled render exception

### `src/main.jsx`
- Wraps `<App />` in `<ErrorBoundary>` so any render-time exception is caught at the root

### `src/App.jsx`
- Added `.catch()` to the bare `getDoc(userRef).then(...)` call — Firestore permission/network errors were silently producing unhandled Promise rejections

### `apps/mobile/services/firebase/firestoreSessionRepository.ts`
- Replaced all `getMobileFirebaseServices()!` (TypeScript non-null assertion, no runtime safety) with a `getServices()` private helper that throws a descriptive `Error` if the value is null
- Affected: `sessionsCol`, `messagesCol`, `deleteSession`, `deleteMessage`, `clearMessages`

```ts
// before — crashes with opaque "Cannot read properties of null"
const services = getMobileFirebaseServices()!;

// after — throws early with a clear message
private getServices(): MobileFirebaseServices {
  const services = getMobileFirebaseServices();
  if (!services) throw new Error('Firebase services are not available');
  return services;
}
```

Two runtime crash vectors identified and patched: malformed localStorage data crashing the app on load, and an unguarded `AudioContext` constructor propagating exceptions into `handleSend`.

## Changes

### `src/MainApp.tsx` — localStorage structure validation (critical)
- `JSON.parse` on stored data can succeed yet return a structurally invalid object (e.g. `roomOrder: null` from older app versions or storage corruption)
- `storage.roomOrder.map(...)` in the `rooms` useMemo would then throw unconditionally, crashing the app before any UI renders
- Added an inline type-guard after parse; falls back to the default empty state if the shape is invalid:

```ts
const candidate: unknown = JSON.parse(historyVal);
if (
  candidate !== null && typeof candidate === 'object' &&
  !Array.isArray(candidate) &&
  typeof (candidate as Record<string, unknown>).rooms === 'object' && ...
  Array.isArray((candidate as Record<string, unknown>).roomOrder)
) {
  parsedStorage = candidate as typeof parsedStorage;
}
```

### `src/lib/audio.ts` — AudioContext constructor safety (medium)
- `new AudioContextClass()` was not wrapped in try-catch; a browser exception (resource limits, security policy) would propagate out of `getAudioContext()`, which is called **outside** the try block in `handleSend` and `handleSwitch`, resulting in an unhandled rejection
- Wrapped the constructor call in try-catch with a `console.warn`

PR #46 broke the login page while adding empresas CRUD and dropdown selectors. This reverts `admin.html` to its last working state and applies only the originally requested change: department is optional for jefe users.

- **Revert**: Full restore of `templates/admin.html` to the state at `ff038d9` (before PR #46 merge)
- **Dept validation fix**: Department selection is now only required when `rol === 'empleado'`, not based on the logged-in user's role (`esJefe`)

```js
// Before: required dept if logged-in user is jefe (wrong semantics)
if (esJefe && _modalDepts.length === 0) { ... }

// After: required dept only for empleado role being created
if (rol === 'empleado' && _modalDepts.length === 0) { ... }
```

